#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 136 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object takes a time value in seconds and formats
it as a human-readable time string in the form "HH:MM:SS" (or "HH:MM:SS.XXX"
if the @ms flag is set). By default the result is output as a string
object (that is \, a symbol in Pd terms); with the @symbol flag \,
the result is sent through the outlet as a symbol. This is the inverse
operation of [conv.str2sec].;
